1
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,833
Dear May Deer,

2
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:11,667
With a lovely family,

3
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:15,250
Dreaming of growing up each day.

4
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,167
Shy Chuan-Chuan Pangolin,

5
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:18,667
Quiet, with not a word to say,

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:19,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

7
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:20,083
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

8
00:00:20,583 --> 00:00:21,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

9
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:22,333
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

10
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:22,917
Don’t be shy!

11
00:00:23,083 --> 00:00:23,917
Don’t be shy!

12
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,500
Sing out loud!

13
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:25,833
Sing out loud!

14
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:27,417
Let your imagination shine!

15
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:31,167
Good friends in the forest,

16
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:33,083
Growing and playing together,

17
00:00:33,083 --> 00:00:34,000
Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan!

18
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,500
ODEER MAYO / Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan

19
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:40,082
The Modern-Day Tooth Fairy

20
00:00:40,917 --> 00:00:45,167
At dinner, May was eating very slowly and looking rather glum.

21
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Mm-hmm.

22
00:00:54,333 --> 00:00:55,083
Yummy!

23
00:00:57,667 --> 00:00:59,917
I have a wobbly tooth in my mouth.

24
00:01:02,583 --> 00:01:05,917
Am I getting old? It hurts when I eat!

25
00:01:06,083 --> 00:01:07,667
Oh, you’re not getting old.

26
00:01:07,667 --> 00:01:09,833
It means you’re about to lose a tooth.

27
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:10,833
You can wait for it to fall out on its own,

28
00:01:10,833 --> 00:01:13,333
or we can visit the dentist and have it pulled.

29
00:01:13,667 --> 00:01:15,417
Pull it out? Pull it out?

30
00:01:18,250 --> 00:01:19,583
No, no, no, no!

31
00:01:19,583 --> 00:01:21,667
I’ll wait for it to fall out by itself.

32
00:01:22,667 --> 00:01:25,250
Then just eat normally, chew your food, and brush your teeth.

33
00:01:27,833 --> 00:01:28,750
Okay, watch me!

34
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:33,583
Ouch! That hurts!

35
00:01:33,583 --> 00:01:34,750
Hehe, May.

36
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:36,583
Do you remember the Tooth Fairy story?

37
00:01:36,583 --> 00:01:37,750
The Tooth Fairy?

38
00:01:38,167 --> 00:01:39,000
Is she the little fairy in the story

39
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,167
who appears when you get a new tooth?

40
00:01:42,167 --> 00:01:43,000
That’s right.

41
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,833
If you put your baby tooth under your pillow,

42
00:01:45,833 --> 00:01:48,250
the Tooth Fairy will leave you a gold coin as a reward.

43
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:49,667
Hooray!

44
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:52,750
Then I have to make my tooth fall out quickly

45
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:54,750
so I can meet the Tooth Fairy!

46
00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:57,500
May chewed her cookies extra hard,

47
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:59,750
and sucked her milk extra hard, too.

48
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:03,000
She brushed her teeth extra hard, but…

49
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Ouch!

50
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:07,750
I’ll just brush them a little, then.

51
00:02:08,167 --> 00:02:10,000
As long as I brush them a bit, that’s enough.

52
00:02:10,417 --> 00:02:12,083
Time for bed!

53
00:02:12,583 --> 00:02:15,417
May, did your tooth fall out?

54
00:02:15,417 --> 00:02:16,833
Not yet, Mom.

55
00:02:16,917 --> 00:02:18,833
My wobbly tooth is like the musical note “Rei.”

56
00:02:18,833 --> 00:02:22,667
It’s stuck to the first line of the music staff and won’t fall off. How annoying!

57
00:02:22,667 --> 00:02:24,583
Come here. Open your mouth and let Mom take a look.

58
00:02:31,667 --> 00:02:32,583
Oh, wonderful!

59
00:02:32,583 --> 00:02:34,500
Mom! My wobbly tooth fell out!

60
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:35,583
Toothie!

61
00:02:35,583 --> 00:02:38,167
I can get a Tooth Fairy coin tonight!

62
00:02:38,167 --> 00:02:39,250
Yeah!

63
00:02:40,333 --> 00:02:42,917
May, why is there a little chip in your tooth?

64
00:02:42,917 --> 00:02:44,250
Have you been brushing your teeth properly?

65
00:02:44,250 --> 00:02:45,167
Oh…

66
00:02:45,167 --> 00:02:47,167
Haha, it’s okay. I’ll brush better next time.

67
00:02:48,333 --> 00:02:50,083
I’ll get my coin tonight!

68
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:53,333
Oh, you’re impossible.

69
00:02:54,833 --> 00:02:56,583
Good night.

70
00:02:59,250 --> 00:03:01,083
I wonder what the Tooth Fairy looks like.

71
00:03:01,083 --> 00:03:02,583
Is she a tiny fairy?

72
00:03:02,583 --> 00:03:04,250
Or does she look just like me?

73
00:03:09,333 --> 00:03:10,583
Wake me up when the Tooth Fairy comes!

74
00:03:10,583 --> 00:03:13,417
Little Deer was already asleep.

75
00:03:13,417 --> 00:03:16,917
May fell asleep, too, while waiting excitedly.

76
00:03:21,583 --> 00:03:23,250
Yaaawn!

77
00:03:23,250 --> 00:03:25,417
Oh! How did I fall asleep?

78
00:03:25,583 --> 00:03:27,750
Did the Tooth Fairy come or not?

79
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:33,500
There’s no coin, but there’s a letter!

80
00:03:33,583 --> 00:03:35,000
I’ll ask Mom to read it.

81
00:03:35,333 --> 00:03:36,583
Mom! Mom!

82
00:03:36,583 --> 00:03:37,583
Good morning, May!

83
00:03:37,583 --> 00:03:39,167
The Tooth Fairy didn’t leave me a coin,

84
00:03:39,167 --> 00:03:40,917
but she left me a letter.

85
00:03:40,917 --> 00:03:42,583
Okay, let’s see.

86
00:03:43,667 --> 00:03:46,917
Dear May, I’m the Tooth Fairy from the Tooth Bank.

87
00:03:46,917 --> 00:03:48,667
I’ve received your tooth.

88
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:51,583
But after our bank’s inspection,

89
00:03:51,583 --> 00:03:53,750
we found that your wobbly tooth wasn’t very well cared for.

90
00:03:54,083 --> 00:03:56,250
It had milk and cookie crumbs on it,

91
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:58,500
and cavity bugs had moved in!

92
00:03:58,833 --> 00:04:01,500
So we can’t give you a coin this time.

93
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,917
I watered it a little, and your new tooth will grow in soon.

94
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:08,583
As long as you brush carefully and take good care of your teeth,

95
00:04:08,917 --> 00:04:12,667
you’ll definitely get a coin next time. Keep it up!

96
00:04:12,667 --> 00:04:15,417
May, it looks like you didn’t get a coin this time.

97
00:04:15,917 --> 00:04:18,167
Oh! It’s because I didn’t brush properly.

98
00:04:18,167 --> 00:04:20,083
That’s why I didn’t get a coin.

99
00:04:20,083 --> 00:04:22,583
I thought that if it didn’t hurt, my teeth were clean.

100
00:04:22,583 --> 00:04:25,500
I didn’t know the cavity bugs had already moved in!

101
00:04:25,583 --> 00:04:27,500
It’s okay, May.

102
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:29,250
The Tooth Fairy is just worried about you.

103
00:04:29,250 --> 00:04:32,417
Just brush your teeth properly, and you’ll get a coin next time.

104
00:04:32,667 --> 00:04:35,167
Okay, Little Deer. We have to brush our teeth well!

105
00:04:35,167 --> 00:04:35,750
Toothie!

106
00:04:36,333 --> 00:04:38,417
May started brushing carefully.

107
00:04:38,417 --> 00:04:40,333
She rinsed her mouth after every meal

108
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:45,250
to make her teeth sparkle like diamonds.

109
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:54,333
I-I lost another tooth!

110
00:04:54,333 --> 00:04:57,500
Mom! I lost another tooth!

111
00:04:57,500 --> 00:05:00,833
Oh, May! Another one of your baby teeth fell out!

112
00:05:00,833 --> 00:05:02,583
Remember to put it under your pillow tonight.

113
00:05:02,667 --> 00:05:04,167
I hope you get a good result!

114
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:07,833
Okay, Little Deer. We’re sure to succeed this time!

115
00:05:13,917 --> 00:05:17,667
Mom! The Tooth Fairy sent another letter! Please open it for me!

116
00:05:17,667 --> 00:05:20,250
Dear May, congratulations on losing another tooth!

117
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:24,500
This time, the Tooth Bank has certified your tooth as flawless.

118
00:05:24,917 --> 00:05:27,750
You’ve been taking such good care of your teeth. Wonderful!

119
00:05:28,333 --> 00:05:31,833
We’re including the coin from last time and awarding you Tooth Fairy coins.

120
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:32,750
Two coins!

121
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:35,083
Love, the Tooth Fairy.

122
00:05:35,083 --> 00:05:37,500
Wow! Two gold coins! That’s wonderful!

123
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,167
Little Deer, one is for you.

124
00:05:39,333 --> 00:05:41,167
Shiny, shiny, shiny!

125
00:05:41,583 --> 00:05:45,167
So when you brush well, losing a tooth doesn’t hurt!

126
00:05:45,417 --> 00:05:47,833
Congratulations! Keep it up!

127
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,333
And you can earn two gold coins!

128
00:05:50,583 --> 00:05:53,583
I’ll take good care of my teeth from now on. This is great!

129
00:05:53,917 --> 00:05:56,167
Teeth, sparkling bright!
